<title>JAPAN: Sakura says securities appraisal loss at Y208 bln.</title>
<headline>Sakura says securities appraisal loss at Y208 bln.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Sakura Bank Ltd said on Tuesday that its appraisal loss on securities holdings was 208 billion yen as of March 31, 1997.  </p>
<p>The major Japanese bank also said in a statement that it forecast a parent operating profit of 280 billion yen for the business year which ended last month.</p>
<p>Sakura said it would incur a 500 billion yen loss for the business year stemming from its planned write-offs of problem loans.</p>
</text>
